    pr_ref:  # 049d
    description: "Found 2026-10-26 while fixing WI-rilof, on dev e22b97d62c through the production CLI. Fixture: a.js `const { helper } = require('./b'); function run() { return helper(); }`, b.js defines helper. `hypergumbo survey` publishes BOTH a.js -> javascript:b.js:1-1:file:file (the js_module linker's resolved imports edge) AND a.js -> javascript:./b:0-0:module:external_symbol, a tier-3 'unresolved external reference' node standing for the in-tree file b.js. The analyzer's raw imports edge (dst javascript:./b:0-0:module:module) is never retired once the linker resolves it, so finalize mints the stub. Same for every resolved alias import and, after WI-rilof, every resolved workspace-package import (javascript:@ws/b:0-0:module:external_symbol). Consequences: one import counted twice (once in-tree, once external), an in-tree file represented by a tier-3 external node (INV-kutub's 'every node standing for one package/file carries one tier'), and the external_symbol population inflated on every JS/TS repo. Fix: when js_module resolves an import edge, retarget that edge (or drop it in favour of the resolved one) instead of adding a parallel edge; check consumers that count imports edges (dependency linker requirements, sketch, supply-chain summary). Measure the stub count on a corpus repo first. Not checked: dynamic imports, CSS/asset imports, TS `import type`."  # 049d
    fields: {}  # 049d
